<html>

<head>
  <script type="application/jay-data">data:</script>
  <!-- REGION-NOT-LINKED (DL#200): the Card import carries only contract= — no template=. A design-system
       template DOES exist for this contract (../../components/card/card.jay-html), so this hand-authored
       <jay:card> could be a managed design-system element instead. `jay-stack validate` warns once per
       region type, suggesting you add template= + run `jay-stack sync`. For a deliberate one-off, suppress
       on the import with jay-validations="REGION-NOT-LINKED" (or list Card under allow-inline-region). -->
  <script type="application/jay-headless" contract="../../components/card/card.jay-contract"></script>
  <title>Design System Demo — Not Linked</title>
  <meta name="description"
    content="A hand-authored <jay:card> region whose import has no template= — REGION-NOT-LINKED.">
  <style>
    .ds-card {
      border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 20px;
      background: #ffffff;
    }

    .ds-card__heading {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      color: #0f172a;
    }

    .ds-card__body {
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      color: #475569;
    }

    .ds-button {
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 8px 14px;
      background: #2563eb;
      color: #ffffff;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <div>
    <p>Not linked: the Card import has no template=, so this card region's body is hand-authored —
      jay-stack validate raises REGION-NOT-LINKED because a shared card template exists.</p>
    <jay:card heading="Starter" body="Everything you need to get going." ctaLabel="Choose Starter">
      <div class="ds-card">
        <h3 class="ds-card__heading">{heading}</h3>
        <p class="ds-card__body">{body}</p>
        <button class="ds-button">{ctaLabel}</button>
      </div>
    </jay:card>
  </div>
</body>

</html>
